based compensation of $420K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 382\u00d7 revenue per employee (very high relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Tiptree Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $640M market cap on $488,000 of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -93% over the past three years and -49% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are contracting by -799.8pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 8% cost of capital, a 3-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $168M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 34471 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.82\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, thin -1.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.4%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 2324% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 40% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -799.8pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 150% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Revenue growth in 